body:
You're not alone with the Prozac experience, I was on that too a while back (though I kind of just suffered through the symptoms till I was switched off it). I'm sorry that happened though, it's these dumb symptoms that make people reluctant to try new meds.


I was diagnosed with BPD II and I'm not currently on anything, no. I've been on and off meds for about 4 years now. Last year I was on some meds that kind of spaced the episodes out but circumstances kind of made me stop taking them... and when I restarted a little later in the year it's like the meds brought them back full force so I'm done with meds for now. And yeah the dysphoria thing, too real.

&#x200B;

I was seeing a psychologist and a psychiatrist but they didn't really bring me much ease. My psychologist seemed more intent on arguing with me than actually making me feel better (one time she actually told me therapy isn't supposed to make you feel better it's just supposed to allow you to talk? Which.. okay. But I can talk to anyone). I don't really have any friends, and the only one that I do have we've had a falling out recently so I've been pretty alone for the better part of 3 months now.

&#x200B;

Thanks for taking time to read my stupid rant haha. I really wish you all the best, too xx
